Doug Freyburger <dfreybur@yahoo.com> deserves a cookie for saying:
> Being a step further from cursed is already covered.  This is not a big
> deal in the early game, but by the time I reach the drawbridge of the
> castle I want all of my weapons and armor blessed because from there on
> it is likely to face spellcasting monsters that can hit.  If one of their
> spells hits a blessed piece of armor, it becomes uncursed.  If uncursed
> it becomes cursed.  If cursed the item vanishes. 

Of course, that's not true.  Spellcasting monsters can curse your
inventory with malignant auras, yes.  A random selection (and number) of
items in your inventory is moved one step down from blessed to uncursed
to cursed.  However, a malignant aura will never destroy anything.

You may be confusing the Curse Items spell with the Destroy Armor spell,
which is an entirely separate thing.  Spellcasting monsters can cast
Destroy Armor, which disintegrates a piece of your armor if you don't
have MR and the armor doesn't resist.  It has nothing to do with cursing
or malignant auras, though.

